cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use ECHO, please cite this software record (CITATION.cff).
type: software
title: "ECHO: sequential experiment selection under uncertainty"
abstract: >-
  ECHO is research software for sequential experiment selection when a
  scientific system is only partially understood and the experimental
  budget is small. It compares acquisition policies on synthetic
  (and user-supplied) hidden systems using paired seeds, multiple
  discovery metrics, failure records, and evaluator-only ground truth.
  No language model is used. This record cites the software. It is not
  a peer-reviewed paper.
